From: FirebirdTA01 <FirebirdTA01@aol.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:33:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/39] expmed: store_bit_field_using_insv gives up on a
 register it cannot view in the insv mode

The SUBREG case already returns false when validate_subreg refuses; the
REG case called gen_lowpart_SUBREG unconditionally.  Since validate_subreg
checks hard registers with simplify_subreg_regno (can_change_mode_class),
SPU returning a complex float in $3 (SCmode, 8 bytes; insv works in a
16-byte mode, which SPU cannot change to) asserted in gen_rtx_SUBREG.
GCC 9.5 accepted it (subreg_offset_representable_p only).
---
 gcc/expmed.cc | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/expmed.cc b/gcc/expmed.cc
index d57ea78d6b1..36911f03e25 100644
--- a/gcc/expmed.cc
+++ b/gcc/expmed.cc
@@ -641,7 +641,16 @@ store_bit_field_using_insv (const extraction_insn *insv, rtx op0,
 				 SUBREG_BYTE (xop0));
 	}
       if (REG_P (xop0) && GET_MODE (xop0) != op_mode)
-	xop0 = gen_lowpart_SUBREG (op_mode, xop0);
+	{
+	  /* As for a SUBREG above: give up if the target cannot view the
+	     register in OP_MODE (a hard register whose class cannot change
+	     between the two modes no longer passes validate_subreg).  */
+	  if (!validate_subreg (op_mode, GET_MODE (xop0), xop0,
+				subreg_lowpart_offset (op_mode,
+						       GET_MODE (xop0))))
+	    return false;
+	  xop0 = gen_lowpart_SUBREG (op_mode, xop0);
+	}
     }
 
